-- §3 an empty matching set at an effect-indexed head, #3689's own repro.
-- `do` desugars to `Thenable` and `pure 1` asks for `Applicative`, both at
-- `Async <Stdout>`.  stdlib/async.mdk implements only the `Deferred*` family
-- for `Async`, so `match(IE, Thenable (Async <Stdout>))` and
-- `match(IE, Applicative (Async <Stdout>))` are empty.
-- Hand-derived: REJECT on all three verbs, `T-NO-IMPL`.  The wanted predicate
-- carries an effect row, which given matching (`monoSameGiven`) erases as
-- coherence does; before that the row never equalled itself and the
-- method-return validator panicked, unlocated, before any diagnostic.
import async.{runAsyncMain, liftIO, spawnTask, await}

main = runAsyncMain (do
  t <- spawnTask (pure 1)
  x <- await t
  liftIO (_ => println x))
